127	// Both possible parents are recorded: HEAD for an ordinary commit and HEAD's
128	// parent for an amend. git's source word cannot tell them apart (`--amend -m`
129	// reports "message", `-C <rev>` reports "commit"), and post-commit sees the
130	// real parent.
